---
alwaysApply: true
---
Use functional components with TypeScript and the latest React best practices.

Always use server components by default in Next.js 13+ unless interactivity is needed.

Use shadcn/ui for accessible, headless UI components; follow its patterns and customization practices.

Ensure visual consistency with Tailwind utility classes (rounded-2xl, shadow-md, p-4, text-sm, etc.).

Optimize for accessibility (ARIA labels, focus outlines, alt text for images).

Structure files using atomic design (components/, pages/, utils/, hooks/, etc.).

Handle forms using react-hook-form + zod for type-safe validation.

Prefer server-side data fetching (getServerSideProps, app router, server actions) over client-side useEffect.

Ensure mobile responsiveness using Tailwind breakpoints (sm:, md:, lg:).

Add framer-motion transitions for modals, dropdowns, and loading states for a smooth UX.

Keep code DRY and modular; extract repeated logic into custom hooks and utilities.

Follow Git best practices: clear commit messages, use feature branches, require PR reviews.